id: pm-evidence-portable-bundles
title: Transfer selected retained citations as validated portable bundles
description: "Export selected evidence artifacts with exact hashes, source descriptors, explicit sharing consent and omission policy. Validate complete bundles and explicit revision-bound target authorization before inspecting or importing."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: backlog-1021,portable-bundles
created_at: "2026-10-28T20:14:00.476Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T20:50:42.169Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Tampered bytes refuse before writes; export excludes unselected sources; a no-git recipient replays retained fragments without original files; revoked consent prevents new export; 500 seeded model sequences compare native SDK read-back; packed npm and Bun acceptance; unchanged full release thresholds
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T20:14:06.625Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: installed CLI SDK declarations expose native history replay, output receipts, fenced mutateItem, complete reads and artifact deduplication, but no retained citation transport. Existing pm-evidence replay requires a citation already on an item; pm-memory import/export transfers knowledge records and guidance, while context/review/rlm consume evidence. This feature transports explicitly selected evidence fragments and source identity on existing native items; no tracker creation or generic archive. Reuse citationSchema, replay, Store and SDK fenced mutation; preserve native relationships and unrelated fields. No pm-evidence entry exists in the older no-git audit, so direct non-git acceptance is required."
  "2026-10-28T20:27:16.862Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explicit sharing grant/revoke, bounded hash-verified retained artifact bundles, compact CLI receipts and SDK inspect/import APIs. All transfer authorization and unchanged decisions read current native state under SDK fenced leases, using verified native history generation to reject ABA and stale retries; preview and apply share one planner. Target foreign evidence is preserved with a typed skip. Focused bundle and command tests pass; new bundle modules measured 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines in the focused coverage run. Public snapshot at 2224762: 15 items, 37 read-only files verified unchanged, 6 cited artifacts, 5 explicitly exported, 1 excluded, 3964 bundle bytes, 360 retained bytes, 5 source-free SDK replays, zero retry additions, tamper refusal and revoked export refusal; metadata inspection 502 estimated tokens."
  "2026-10-28T20:35:01.314Z",codex-agent,"Validation: 9 focused bundle/CLI/concurrency tests pass, including the pm test --run --only-index 1 --progress journey (result tracking is disabled by project policy; result recorded here). Seed 0xb0d1e2026 passed 500 sequences / 2000 operations / 2000 SDK target read-backs on 25 trackers: 109 imports, 555 unchanged replays, 67 sharing refusals and 512 validated producer bundles. Native parent/dependency edges, custom active/blocked statuses and ambient focus were exercised. Five isolated function-only negative controls each failed exactly one behavioral test: checksum, explicit selection, native generation authorization, live sharing consent and retained bytes; restored disposable implementation passed 4/4. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates pass. No local full release suite was launched; full npm/Bun evidence will come from exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-28T20:36:55.856Z",codex-agent,"Overlap additionally verified against the installed current 2026.10.28 CLI SDK declarations: native history/evidence reads exist, no retained-citation transport API. Local health reports only extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew from an inherited newer pm-github extension outside this package; settings, storage, integrity and history drift checks pass. No global configuration or telemetry changes were made. CI uses the pinned host on a clean runner and remains the authoritative full health/release gate. Filesystem no-git support is verified; remote atomic mutation conformance remains explicitly outside the existing backend-conformance item scope."
  "2026-10-28T20:37:52.731Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passes 2/2 journeys: npm/npx and Bun/bunx, project-local executables, embedded SDK and both global pm installs all exercise bundle transport and unchanged retry. Remote atomic mutation conformance is outside this feature and remains tracked by pm-evidence-backend-conformance; no new SDK gap was encountered. The ready review PR will use CI npm release gates on Node 22 and 26 plus the Bun gate on Node 26 at unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero duplication thresholds. All later gate results will be linked in the PR, preserving final-head tracker history."
  "2026-10-28T20:44:40.271Z",codex-agent,"Final review follow-through: add a persisted retained citation fixture produced by the released baseline, extend sharing/consent boundary interleavings, and verify that CLI file reads consume one complete unchanged bounded snapshot before parsing. These strengthen the compatibility and complete-input acceptance contracts while CI remains queued."
  "2026-10-28T20:50:39.627Z",codex-agent,"Follow-through verified: 12/12 focused tests pass; both new bundle modules remain measured at 100/100/100/100 in focused coverage. Six isolated function-only controls each fail exactly one test (including complete CLI input snapshot); restored implementation passes 5/5 bundle tests. Added exact native evidence state emitted by the released v2026.10.28 producer with synthetic CRLF source: it reads/replays unchanged, refuses unconsented export, and exports after a grant. Eight import plus eight sharing/consent interleavings and an actual held-lease competing writer pass. CLI rejects incomplete reads and same-size file edits before parsing. Final model assertions now also compare complete origin/provenance, normalized SDK artifact links, native comment text/author and review attribution. CI run 40765210411 on initial head remains queued; final follow-up head requires fresh exact-head CI. The original 30-minute CI waiting cutoff remains in effect."
